<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L469" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">To overlay the two plots, we use the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:plots,display" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">display</Font></Hyperlink> command, which is part of the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:plots" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">plots</Font></Hyperlink> package.  In its simplest form, this command accepts a list of plot structures (such as what you obtain by applying the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:plot" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">plot</Font></Hyperlink> command) and overlays the plots.  It can also accept most of the options that are available for <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:plot" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">plot</Font></Hyperlink>.  Below, we demonstrate the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:plots,display" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">display</Font></Hyperlink> command along with the use of several options to provide an informative graph.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L470" drawlabel="true">
